 # Registry Specifications
 
-- [ ] **REG-001**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL normalize surrounding whitespace and ASCII letter case before returning a matching record or NotFound.
-- [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
+- [ ] **REG-001**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL normalize surrounding whitespace and uppercase ASCII letters A-Z before returning a matching record or NotFound; every other character SHALL be left unchanged.
+- [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes on a kiosk with an active snapshot, the system SHALL include that snapshot's date in the result, whether or not a matching record was found.
 - [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
 - [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a snapshot passes validation, the system SHALL build a local SQLite index containing every record in that snapshot before activating the snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When building the local index fails, including insufficient disk space, the system SHALL reject the import and keep the previously activated snapshot and index in service.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL answer it from the local index of the active snapshot without contacting a network service.
+- [ ] **REG-008**: When a serial-number lookup is requested and the kiosk has no usable active index, the system SHALL report that no snapshot is available rather than returning NotFound.
+- [ ] **REG-009**: When a snapshot record is not valid JSON, is missing a required field, has an empty required field, or has an empty canonical serial number, the system SHALL reject the import and keep the previously activated snapshot and index in service.
+- [ ] **REG-010**: When a snapshot import fails, the system SHALL report the reason to the operator, naming the offending record or serial number for a content failure and the snapshot version for an unsupported version.
+- [ ] **REG-011**: When a snapshot is imported, the system SHALL store each serial number in canonical form (surrounding whitespace removed, ASCII letters A-Z uppercased) and SHALL treat two records with equal canonical serial numbers as duplicates.
+- [ ] **REG-012**: When a serial-number lookup is requested on a kiosk with 4 GB of RAM and an active index of up to 90,000 records, the system SHALL return the result within 250 ms.
+- [ ] **REG-013**: While a snapshot import is in progress, the system SHALL continue to serve lookups from the previously activated index.
+- [ ] **REG-014**: When the kiosk starts, the system SHALL discard temporary and superseded index and snapshot files and SHALL keep serving lookups from the active index.
+- [ ] **REG-015**: When the snapshot's signature does not cover the snapshot's record content, the system SHALL reject the import and keep the previously activated snapshot and index in service.
+- [ ] **REG-016**: When an import is requested while another import is in progress, the system SHALL refuse the new import, report the refusal to the operator, and leave the running import unaffected.
+- [ ] **REG-017**: When a snapshot is imported, the system SHALL take the snapshot date from the snapshot rather than from the kiosk clock.
+- [ ] **REG-018**: When a snapshot is activated, the system SHALL retain that snapshot file on the kiosk and remove the previously activated snapshot file.
+- [ ] **REG-019**: When a lookup is in progress when a new snapshot is activated, the system SHALL return the record and snapshot date from the index that the lookup opened.
+- [ ] **REG-020**: When a snapshot's snapshot date is missing or is not an ISO 8601 calendar date, the system SHALL reject the import and keep the previously activated snapshot and index in service.
